--- !u!114 &997651622
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 997651621}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 75f86c6bb80f37c4c844542be0db158a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FarmerGameController
  openButton: {fileID: 281939086}
  openOnStart: 1
  showTestButton: 1
  farmerIllustration: {fileID: 0}
  ananseIllustration: {fileID: 0}
  ananseNoPotIllustration: {fileID: 0}
  characterHeight: 900
  font: {fileID: 0}
  backgroundOpacity: 0
  cameraDim: 0.3
  ananseBrokenPotIllustration: {fileID: 0}
  gameOverLine: Aaah! My pots! The farmer's knowledge spills into the dirt... I must learn it all again.
  crops:
  - id: yam
    displayName: Yam
  - id: cassava
    displayName: Cassava
  - id: plantain
    displayName: Plantain
  - id: maize
    displayName: Maize
  - id: beans
    displayName: Beans
  - id: rice
    displayName: Rice
  - id: cocoa
    displayName: Cocoa
  - id: palmoil
    displayName: Palm Oil
  levels:
  - foodId: kelewele
    displayName: Kelewele
    crops:
    - plantain
    lessonLine: Kelewele. Ripe plantain, spiced with ginger and pepper, then fried.
    fact: Ripe plantain is cut, spiced with ginger and pepper, then fried. A favorite evening street snack.
  - foodId: chocolate
    displayName: Chocolate
    crops:
    - cocoa
    lessonLine: Chocolate. It all starts with cocoa, and Ghana grows some of the best cocoa in the world.
    fact: Ghana is one of the world's largest cocoa producers. The beans are fermented and sun-dried before they become chocolate.
  - foodId: waakye
    displayName: Waakye
    crops:
    - rice
    - beans
    lessonLine: Waakye. Rice and beans, cooked together in one pot.
    fact: Rice and beans are cooked together. The red-brown color comes from dried sorghum leaves.
  - foodId: fufu
    displayName: Fufu
    crops:
    - cassava
    - plantain
    lessonLine: Fufu. We boil cassava and plantain, then pound them together.
    fact: Cassava and plantain are boiled, then pounded in a mortar and eaten with soup.
  - foodId: banku
    displayName: Banku
    crops:
    - maize
    - cassava
    lessonLine: Banku. Corn dough and cassava dough, stirred over the fire.
    fact: Fermented corn dough and cassava dough are stirred over the fire, often served with pepper and grilled tilapia.
  - foodId: ampesi
    displayName: Ampesi
    crops:
    - yam
    - plantain
    lessonLine: Yam and plantain ampesi. Boiled, and eaten with kontomire stew.
    fact: Yam and plantain are boiled and eaten with kontomire (cocoyam leaf) stew.
  - foodId: gobe
    displayName: Gobe
    crops:
    - beans
    - palmoil
    - plantain
    - cassava
    lessonLine: Gobe. Beans in palm oil, with gari from cassava and fried plantain.
    fact: Beans are cooked in palm oil and served with gari (roasted grated cassava) and fried plantain.
  introDialogue:
  - speaker: 0
    text: Ah, Kwaku Ananse! You have walked a long way. Welcome to my farm.
    anansePose: 0
  - speaker: 0
    text: Everything we eat in Ghana begins in the soil. Yam, cassava, plantain, maize, beans, rice, cocoa, palm nut.
    anansePose: 0
  - speaker: 1
    text: The farmer's knowledge... it will look good in my pot.
    anansePose: 0
  - speaker: 0
    text: Sit with me. I will show you what each crop becomes.
    anansePose: 0
  preGameDialogue:
  - speaker: 0
    text: Now show me what you learned. Put the right crops under each food.
    anansePose: 0
  - speaker: 1
    text: Careful. Every mistake cracks a pot. Three broken pots and the knowledge is gone.
    anansePose: 0
  winDialogue:
  - speaker: 0
    text: You know my farm now, Ananse. Go well.
    anansePose: 0
  - speaker: 1
    text: The pot is full, and this time it will not break. Now, the carver.
    anansePose: 0
  wrongMessages:
  - No, that one does not belong there.
  - Look again, Ananse.
  - Hmm. Remember what I showed you.
  onOpened:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  onClosed:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  onCompleted:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  returnTitle: WELCOME BACK
  returnLine: A new pot from Nana Nyame. This time I will keep it whole.
