--- !u!114 &2008057260
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2008057259}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 84ea3ff60e831ae4bb9f1ed16db9b9f6, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NanaNyameOffering
  nanaPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  nanaPotArt: {fileID: 0}
  firstVisit:
  - Kwaku Ananse. You climbed all the way up to my sky with a gift?
  - Kente, woven by your own hands. You have shown me gratitude, and gratitude is rare.
  - Take this pot. It is no ordinary pot. Keep it whole.
  secondVisit:
  - Ananse again. Your first pot broke, didn't it?
  - Still, another fine cloth. Here, a new pot. Be more careful this time.
  repeatVisit:
  - Back so soon, little spider? Very well. A cloth for a pot.
  - Your weaving grows better each time. Take your pot.
  - The sky has many pots, Ananse. Try not to break this one.
  strongerPot:
  - Another kente? Your gratitude has no end, Ananse.
  - Let me make your pot stronger.
  fullPotLine: Your pot is as strong as a pot can be, Ananse. Keep your kente for another day.
  firstPotThought: Imagine what I could keep in a pot like this... all the knowledge in the village.
  collectThought: Nana Nyame is holding out a pot for me! I should tap him to take it.
  waitingThought: Nana Nyame is still holding my pot. I should tap him and take it first.
  alreadyHasPotLine: Your pot is still whole, Ananse. Keep your kente for now.
  noKenteLine: Ah, Ananse. It is good to see you.
  dragHintThought: I should give Nana Nyame my kente. I'll drag it from my Bag onto him.
  strongerHintThought: Another kente could make my pot stronger. I'll drag it from my Gifts onto Nana Nyame.
  onPotGranted:
